{{Quote|And who are you, Nite Owl?|Paz Vizsla to Bo-Katan Kryze|<ref name="Ch. 19" />}}
The '''Nite Owls''' were an elite [[Mandalorian]] [[Death Watch Warrior|unit]] made up of [[Soldier|warriors]] led by [[Bo-Katan Kryze]] as part of the larger [[Death Watch]] movement. After [[Maul]] [[Death|killed]] Death Watch leader [[Pre Vizsla]] in battle and proclaimed himself its new leader, the Nite Owls, like the rest of the Death Watch, split in two, with members siding with either Maul or Bo-Katan. Those who joined Bo-Katan became part of the [[Mandalore resistance]] and fought against Maul's [[Shadow Collective]] and his [[Mandalorian super commando]]s. They even attempted to free Bo-Katan's sister, the former [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]] of [[Mandalore]], whom they had formerly opposed due to her pacifist idealism. The Nite Owls would survive the [[Clone Wars]] and persist into both the [[Imperial Era|Imperial]] and [[New Republic Era]]s.

==History==
===Death Watch===
{{Quote|No outsider will ever rule Mandalore!|Bo-Katan Kryze, before leaving Death Watch with her Nite Owls|<ref name="Shades of Reason" />}}
The Nite Owls<ref name="Eminence gallery">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/eminence-episode-gallery|text="Eminence" Episode Gallery}}</ref> were a group of elite [[Mandalorian warrior]]s who were a part of the extremist group known as the [[Death Watch]]. Led by [[Bo-Katan Kryze]], who served under Death Watch leader [[Pre Vizsla]], the group were amongst the former [[governor]]'s forces at his [[Carlac Death Watch camp|camp]] on [[Carlac]] during the [[Clone Wars]] after the group abandoned<ref name="A Friend in Need" /> their [[Deathwatch hideout|hideout]] on [[Concordia]].<ref name="Duchess">{{TCW|Duchess of Mandalore}}</ref> In [[20 BBY]], the Nite Owls raided a [[Ming Po]] [[Ming Po Town|settlement]], abducting women and burning buildings. Soon after, they chased away the [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]], who had been their prisoner before escaping with [[Lux Bonteri]].<ref name="A Friend in Need" />

[[File:MandaloreResistance-TL.png|thumb|left|250px|Bo-Katan and her Nite Owls rescue Obi-Wan Kenobi]]
After the rogue [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] and his brother [[Savage Opress]] allied themselves with the Death Watch, forming the [[Shadow Collective]], the Nite Owls were one of the groups among their considerable forces prepared to retake Mandalore from the pacifist [[New Mandalorians]], who ruled the planet via Bo-Katan's sister, the [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]]. However, after the successful [[Takeover of Mandalore|takeover]], Maul [[Death|killed]] Pre Vizsla in a duel and assumed leadership of the Death Watch. Many members of the Death Watch felt that they were honor-bound to serve Maul, as he had defeated their previous leader fairly in combat; however, some of the Nite Owls and other members of the Death Watch disagreed. Declaring that "no outsider will ever rule Mandalore," Bo-Katan escaped in the aftermath of Maul's murder of Vizsla, alongside some of the Nite Owls.<ref name="The Lawless" />

Afterward, Bo-Katan would help Duchess Satine and later Jedi [[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] escape Mandalore and alert the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] to what happened with her newly-formed [[Mandalore resistance]]. The two sisters and their forces joined together to thwart Maul's new reign during a [[Mandalorian Civil War (19 BBY)|civil war]]. However, their efforts were unsuccessful and ended with Satine's execution at the hands of Maul. Although Maul was later imprisoned by [[Darth Sidious]],<ref name="The Lawless" /> his puppet leader, [[Almec]], continued to publicly rule Mandalore,<ref name="OFNF">{{TCW|Old Friends Not Forgotten}}</ref> and some members of the Nite Owls eventually left the planet in search of a way to dislodge Almec from the throne.<ref name="Dangerous Debt">{{TCW|Dangerous Debt}}</ref>

===Reclaiming Mandalore===
[[File:BoKatanKryze-BHUSC.png|thumb|right|180px|The Nite Owls were led by Bo-Katan Kryze.]]
Bo-Katan and fellow Nite Owls member [[Ursa Wren]] would eventually track down the now-former Jedi Ahsoka Tano and enlist her to help them end Maul's rule on Mandalore, who had since escaped from prison and returned to the Mandalorian homeworld. Tano agreed and, despite no longer having ties to the Galactic Republic or its [[Grand Army of the Republic|military]], gathered the newly-formed [[332nd Division]] to bolster the Nite Owls. Together, they laid siege to Mandalore<ref name="OFNF" /> and eventually captured Maul.<ref name="The Phantom Apprentice">{{TCW|The Phantom Apprentice}}</ref> While Tano and part of her contingent of [[clone trooper]]s transported Maul back to [[Coruscant]], Bo-Katan and her Nite Owls remained on Mandalore.<ref name="Shattered">{{TCW|Shattered}}</ref> Bo-Katan was also named [[regent]] of the planet.<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Heroes of Mandalore]]''</ref> However, the execution of [[Order 66]] and the ensuing [[Great Jedi Purge]],<ref name="Shattered" /> collapse of the Republic, and [[Proclamation of the New Order|formation]] of a new [[Galactic Empire]], ensured that bloody turmoil on Mandalore was far from over.<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref>

With the remaining Republic forces stationed on planet,<ref name="Bo-Katan SWCT">{{SWCT|set=2020 Base Series 2|cardname=Bo-Katan Kryze}}</ref> the Empire [[Occupation of Mandalore|occupied]] Mandalore. When the Nite Owls resisted the Empire's rule, Bo-Katan was betrayed by [[Clan Saxon]] and forcefully removed from power, and the Nite Owls once again lost control of Mandalore.<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore" />

===Galactic Civil War===
In 2 BBY, the Nite Owls, along with [[Clan Wren]], [[Clan Vizsla]], [[Clan Rook]], [[Clan Eldar]], and Protector [[Fenn Rau]], aided the [[Spectres]] cell of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], in the destruction of the [[Arc Pulse Generator]] and, with the [[Darksaber]] in her possession, unified under Bo-Katan in another attempt to reclaim Mandalore.<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Heroes of Mandalore]]''</ref> However, the planet was lost again when the Empire retaliated with the bombing of Mandalore, known as the [[Great Purge of Mandalore|Great Purge]].<ref name="Chapter 11">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref> One small crew of Nite Owls remained active on the ruined surface<ref name="Chapter 23">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 23: The Spies}}</ref> and began the work of re-cultivating the world's plant life.<ref name="Chapter 24">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 24: The Return}}</ref>

===Post-Imperial operations===
[[File:NiteOwlCommandos-SWZ91.png|thumb|left|300px|A trio of Nite Owl Commandos]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate}}</ref> Bo-Katan and another member of the Nite Owls, [[Koska Reeves]],<ref name="Chapter 11" /> worked as a [[Bo-Katan Kryze's unit|unit]]<ref name="Mando Sticker">''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian Ultimate Sticker Collection]]''</ref> alongside Mandalorian warrior [[Axe Woves]]. Joined by [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]], they stole and looted an [[Imperial Gozanti-class cruiser|''Gozanti''-class cruiser]] on the [[moon]] of [[Trask]].<ref name="Chapter 11" /> The Nite Owls,<ref name="Chapter 22">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 22: Guns for Hire}}</ref> along with Kryze's other Mandalorian followers, abandoned their leader after she failed to reclaim the Darksaber from [[Gideon's light cruiser]], becoming [[Mercenary|mercenaries]]<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref> under Woves. After Kryze inadvertently reclaimed the right to the darksaber<ref name="Chapter 22" /> during a [[mission to the Living Waters]] with Djarin,<ref name="Chapter 18">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore}}</ref> she took back control of her forces on the planet [[Plazir-15]].<ref name="Chapter 22" />

Putting their differences with the [[Children of the Watch]]-aligned [[The Tribe|Mandalorian tribe]] aside, Kryze's forces, including her Nite Owls, journeyed with the Children to [[Conflict on Mandalore|reclaim]] Mandalore, where they also united with the Nite Owl crew eking out a living on Mandalore.<ref name="Chapter 23" /> Faced with [[Gideon's Imperial remnant]], which had established a base on Mandalore, Kryze and the Armorer led their gathered supporters, including Nite Owls like Reeves, into battle. During the battle Gideon destroyed the Darksaber, however a victory over the Imperial forces was still gained. Mandalore was reclaimed by its people.<ref name="Chapter 24" />

==Equipment==
The Nite Owls wore their [[Nite Owl helmet|distinct]] [[Mandalorian armor]]. They were armed with [[GALAAR-15 blaster carbine]]s before Maul's takeover, while they continued using [[WESTAR-35 blaster pistol]]s with [[Mandalorian vambrace]]s in combat.<ref name="The Lawless">{{TCW|The Lawless}}</ref>

